{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/128692-privateers-vs-loyalists","id":128692,"title":"Privateers vs. Loyalists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-08T19:20:53-07:00","id":128692,"title":"Privateers vs. Loyalists","content":"Hi folks!<br /> <br /> I was going through the Changeling core recently, looking for ideas to further populate my campaign with horrible problems my heroes have to solve, when I was struck with a confusion:<br /> <br /> Essentially, I'm having trouble telling the difference between Privateers and Loyalists. As near as I can tell, the both serve the same niche (capturing other Changelings and sending them back to the fae, either through treachery or force or other methods), but the only difference seems to be their motivations: personal gain vs. loyalty to their Keepers. <br /> <br /> That's all well and good, but that seems a little similar to be counted as distinct antagonists. How have you used them differently? How do you make them distinct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1097-underwoodfive","name":"underwoodfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T19:29:33-07:00","id":128694,"title":"","content":"The latest Hunter supplement Mortal Remains addresses this very thing:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chapter Two: All is Lost, page 44-45</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally speaking, privateers are Lost who use their fae-born abilities to capture, sell, and enslave humans and Changelings. Privateers take their kidnapped victims through the Hedge and sell them to Goblin Market slave stall owners \u2014 or even to the True Fae themselves.<br /> \u200bMost Changelings believe that the only thing worse than a privateer is a loyalist \u2014 a Lost who continues to work for a True Fae\u2019s interests, even after her release back into the human world.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> Not all privateers are loyalists; some Changelings are motivated by profit and hate the True Fae. Not all loyalists are privateers, either; they may also serve the True Fae as spies or exotic goods dealers, too. Those who fall into both groups are the bane of the Lost\u2019s existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T23:34:23-07:00","id":128778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>underwoodfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/128692-privateers-vs-loyalists#post128692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How have you used them differently? How do you make them distinct?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the biggest distinction to that makes it worth having both is the Loyalist that isn't out to drag you back to the True Fae. Rather the Loyalist that has so many things the Lost crave. They aren't hunted, they aren't living in constant fear of their masters, they are allowed to exist full in a world that accepts them instead of hiding.<br /> <br /> They are the temptation of the sacrifice of freedom for comforts. They are dangerous because they are insidious. They aren't going to bother attacking you, or kidnapping your friends. They'll be friendly, and helpful, and nice. All because in the end you'll see that leaving the service of the True Fae has made you miserable and you'll come around on your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T01:15:30-07:00","id":128813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/128692-privateers-vs-loyalists?p=128778#post128778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are the temptation of the sacrifice of freedom for comforts. They are dangerous because they are insidious. They aren't going to bother attacking you, or kidnapping your friends. They'll be friendly, and helpful, and nice. All because in the end you'll see that leaving the service of the True Fae has made you miserable and you'll come around on your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of throwing away freedom in return for comforts is more of a Mage theme than a Changeling one (the Seers come to mind). The main take away would be an unhealthy relationship. Stockholm syndrome between changeling and it's master. The same way a person deal with an abusive SO or parent. They know it's unhealthy, that it may one day kill them, but they keep returning, in the hope that they will gain some sort of approval from their abusive masters. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T01:35:07-07:00","id":128819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/128692-privateers-vs-loyalists?p=128813#post128813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of throwing away freedom in return for comforts is more of a Mage theme than a Changeling one (the Seers come to mind).</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I don't really care if there's thematic overlap in the antagonists of different game lines. There's plenty of that if you go looking. What matters is how it meshes with the themes of Changeling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The main take away would be an unhealthy relationship. </div> </div> </div>Of course. That's why Loyalists are antagonists and bad-guys. I was stressing what makes them dangerous as antagonists (the temptation they offer) rather than why they're completely wrong (their comfort is a complete lie to cover up said unhealthy relationships).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T07:01:43-07:00","id":128919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/128692-privateers-vs-loyalists?p=128694#post128694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all loyalists are privateers, either; they may also serve the True Fae as spies or exotic goods dealers, too</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the biggest reasons I use Loyalists as pure villains; they are 100% working for the True Fae and are doing so for their own gain. They can be working in any capacity, in any location, pretending to be your average Lost on the street or even influential members of the Freeholds. Privateers tend to be my dark heroes, they are motivated by profit and can sometimes do the right thing if there's something in it for them; granted this usually has to deal with buying and selling living intelligent creatures but what else is a Freehold supposed to do with a criminal (like a Loyalist)? If death is too light a punishment, or if they are asking for it, what would be more fitting than to trade them away to a Hob who happens to have a few humans or Changelings caged up in a stockyard? Nobody else would be willing to deal with this creature but a Privateer does on a regular basis, and they get to liberate an innocent or two in the process, and he could charge a fee to the Freehold. Everybody (except the criminal) wins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I ask for so little. Just fear me, <b>love me</b>, do as I say and I will be your slave.<br /> -Jareth, Goblin King","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2846-jhornb02","name":"jhornb02","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2846_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T08:09:03-07:00","id":128966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jhornb02</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/128692-privateers-vs-loyalists?p=128919#post128919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of the biggest reasons I use Loyalists as pure villains; they are 100% working for the True Fae and are doing so for their own gain.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026To the book again:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some loyalists serve out of a misguided sense of duty; others are bound by magical ties, supernatural oaths, or are being coerced in other ways. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T16:29:47-07:00","id":129382,"title":"","content":"My understanding is more that Loyalists are loyal to an individual True Fae (usuall), whether by loyalty, love, fear or something else. They have a reason beyond power and wealth. Privateers aren't necessarily loyal to any True Fae, they're just bastards who'll sell you out for Tokens and Fae promises. You can be both, but most aren't.<br /> <br /> From a storytelling perspective, most Loyalists are sympathetic. Like at Paxton, in the core, who is controlled by fear that she'll be retaken. Like at Maya Sharptongue, from Grim Fears, who considers suicide regularly. Privateers, though? They've been through a durance and know how horrible it and they don't have the excuse of terror/love that most Loyalists have. They're not sympathetic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T19:40:31-07:00","id":137614,"title":"","content":"Super late in responding, but I just wanted to thank everyone for their responses! I think I get the ways to use them differently now, although I find it it interesting that there's a split about which group is the more sympathetic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1097-underwoodfive","name":"underwoodfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}